WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.501
-I'm so happy to have you on.
-I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.167
I hope I don't have to do
a plank or anything.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.634
-No, no, no.
Not everyone has to do --

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.367
-I saw a lot of
physical exercise on this stage.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.033
-This is all just talking
and getting to know each other.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.534
-Great. I love talking.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:14.033
-I -- Congrats on everything.
-Thank you.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:16.367
-What a year for you.

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.267
I want to talk --
Well, can we just talk about

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.701
the single cover?

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:22.534
Is this --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:26.033
The song is giant,
but what is the cover here?

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.467
Is this a real --

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.200
-Yeah, it's my
actual middle finger.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.601
-That's your --
-But -- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.467
That -- You should've seen
that with skin on.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:35.067
It was -- Mnh-mnh.
-But what happened to you?

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.067
-I wish I had this
exciting story of, like,

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:38.467
I was, like,
fighting a bear or something.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.801
-Yeah.
-No.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.567
I -- Literally,
I had to take my dog out,

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:42.968
and it was raining outside.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:44.334
My dog didn't want to
go outside,

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.567
so she was, like,
under my mom's bed.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.501
And so then I rang
the front-door bell,

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.234
and then she,
like, started sprinting

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:51.334
and she started barking.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.334
And then she saw it was me,

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.133
so she went to run
under the bed.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.300
And so I literally started
sprinting after her.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.033
I went to, like,
reach and grab her harness.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.234
I tripped and
fell at the same time

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.334
and I went to catch myself.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.601
I literally
remember looking down

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:04.734
and I caught myself, like --

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:05.934
Like, I don't want to
flip you off.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.067
-No, no. I know.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.234
-But, like,
if you look, she's still --

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.501
-Yes, you're double flipping
me off right now.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.734
-Yeah, you're welcome.

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:13.400
I thought you
needed the comparison, you know?

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.934
-But it turned out it ended up
like this, but with skin on it.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.033
-With skin on it.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.634
It was disgusting.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:22.367
It was terrible.
-So, what happened then?

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.200
You went to the hospital?
-So, I went to the hospital.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.534
My poor mother just had
a knee replacement, right?

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:30.133
Two weeks post-op.
It's just the two of us.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.434
She's trying to drive me.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:33.000
She has a really bad,
like, gag reflex

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.734
if she sees anything
that grosses her out.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:38.200
Like, she'll -- And, so, she was
sitting there dry-heaving,

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.133
and I'm sitting here
and I'm like, "It's my hand!

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.400
This is my hand!

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.367
You don't get to throw up
on my hand!"

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.367
-"Stop talking! Ugh!"

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.133
-And I'm sitting here like,
"I don't know what's going on!

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:50.167
Look away!"

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.200
-Tell me about "abcdefu."

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.501
I mean, it exploded --
Was it TikTok?

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:55.667
Was that where --

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.167
-Yeah, I mean, I would
definitely, like --

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.767
I could definitely take it back
and pinpoint it, I mean,

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:00.334
as much as I can.

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:03.400
All of this is so, like -- The
fact that I'm here, I'm like --

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.100
I've pretended that this --
I've been sitting on this couch

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.334
for like years in my house,
and now I'm here.

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:09.934
Like, that's so --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:12.734
What?
-You're here. You did it.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:16.234
-And it's thanks to this, like,
app on my phone.

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:20.467
Like, I mean, I posted the song.
Like, I had it out.

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:22.701
And, I mean,
it was out for a couple months,

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:23.868
and there's
some videos made to it,

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.734
but, like, not really a lot.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:28.300
And I started seeing --
I really started seeing, like,

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.133
sign language
being connected to the song.

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:31.434
Like, anytime
I heard anything --

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:34.334
Like, the first time I saw
anything being a trend

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:38.200
of anything, it was, like,
putting sign language to "abc."

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.367
And I also -- I thought it was
really exciting just --

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.367
or really cool to have, like,

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:45.067
people to want to learn
sign language

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.334
because of maybe my song
to, like --

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:48.634
That was
really interesting to me,

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.501
And even just, like,
the hard-of-hearing, deaf side

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:53.267
of TikTok really started
and, like,

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:55.234
gave people the ability
to sing that song.

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:57.601
And I'm literally so grateful
for that side of TikTok.

00:02:57.601 --> 00:02:59.434
Like, it literally
started everything.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:01.367
-That's amazing to hear,
'cause, usually,

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:03.434
you hear the other side of
TikTok and social media.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.667
When you hear the good stuff,
it's like no one talks about it.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:06.968
So that's awesome.

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:09.567
I remember hearing it for
the first time on the radio,

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:12.200
and I go,
"Oh, this is a massive song."

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.000
And then I was
asking you about it,

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.234
and you actually have
a video of the first time

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:17.801
you heard your song
on the radio.

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:18.934
-I do. I do.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.067
-And if this doesn't give
you goose bumps --

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.067
Just check this out.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.400
This is real. Check out Gayle.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.367
-"abcdefu."
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.334
-Oh, my God!

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:30.300
-♪ Forget you and your mom ♪

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.601
♪ And your sister and your job ♪

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.634
[ Screams ]

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.167
-It's that move.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.868
It's that move like,
"Is this real?"

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.300
"You're seeing it, too.
You're hearing it, too.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.300
It is real, right?"

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.133
-Oh, my God. So much screaming.

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:46.234
-What can we expect next?
Now, like, we want more.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.567
But we do.

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.167
Let's enjoy this moment
while we have it.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.334
-Yes, I have a song
coming out this month, actually.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.701
-This month.
-This month. January.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:54.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.834
-Gayle, it's a pleasure
to meet you.

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:59.000
-Happy to meet you, yes.
-Man, oh, man, you're talented.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.734
Congrats on everything.
Gayle, everybody.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:05.133
She is performing her song,
"abcdefu," when we come back.

